Fix allowed-failures.txt matcher escaping for test names containing '.'

summarize-tests builds a grep pattern from each FAIL name, escaping regex
metacharacters ('.', '+') via `sed 's/[.+]/\\&/g'`. The command substitution
uses backticks, which strip one backslash level (\\& -> \&) before sed runs, so
sed treats \& as a literal ampersand and REPLACES the '.'/'+' instead of
escaping it. The resulting pattern (e.g. ^conform/ISO/setjmp&h/conform...) never
matches, so every allowed failure whose name contains '.' (all conform/*.h
tests) is reported as an unallowed FAIL and aborts `make check` before the
compiled tests run.

Use $(...) command substitution, which preserves \\& so sed produces the
intended \. escape and the pattern matches.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index a6aabca6..472ed0b7 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -770,7 +770,7 @@ define summarize-tests
 	    case "$$line" in \
 	      FAIL:*) \
 	        name=$${line#FAIL: }; \
-	        escaped_name=`printf '%s' "$$name" | sed 's/[.+]/\\&/g'`; \
+	        escaped_name=$$(printf '%s' "$$name" | sed 's/[.+]/\\&/g'); \
 	        if grep -Eq -- "^$${escaped_name}[[:space:]]*#" \
 	          $(..)allowed-failures.txt; then \
 	          echo "Ignoring allowed FAIL: $${name}"; \
